\": true,\n        \"other\": \"slightly alkaline pH\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"NiS catalyzes addition of H2O to C2H2, yielding acetaldehyde.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"NiS-driven acetylene hydration is experimentally demonstrated as an upstream acetaldehyde source for Strecker. (2023, Communications Chemistry).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_006\",\n      \"name\": \"Electrical-discharge Strecker: CH4/NH3/H2O/H2 \u2192 HCN/acetaldehyde/aminonitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_012\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_007\", \"mol_008\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"high voltage discharge\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Electrical discharge fragments simple molecules; radical and ionic recombination yields HCN, acetaldehyde, and 2-aminopropanenitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Classical Miller\u2013Urey mechanism yields aminonitrile for alanine via atmospheric/surface discharge, robustly supported. (Miller, 1955; Miller, 1957; Johnson et al., 2008; Parker et al., 2011).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_007\",\n      \"name\": \"Classical Strecker synthesis from acetaldehyde\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_007\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_006\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_013\", \"mol_008\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"mildly basic, aqueous\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Acetaldehyde condenses with NH3 to form imine; HCN/CN- attack produces 2-aminopropanenitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Established Strecker amino acid pathway; key hub for varied prebiotic feedstocks. (Miller, 1957, BBA).\"