m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: L-Alanine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: Construct a comprehensive synthesis network for prebiotic L-alanine featuring 10 experimentally defensible distinct pathways, each with unique precursor, environment, and mechanistic context, guided by rigorous literature evidence. The network explicitly distinguishes aminonitrile/Strecker, pyruvate-based reductive amination, transamination, cyanosulfidic/UV network, high-temperature hydrothermal, Fischer\u2013Tropsch-type, exogenous (extraterrestrial/parent body), and formose/ammonia chemistry. All paths converge on DL-alanine, with a separable\u2014currently unestablished\u2014L-enrichment node.\n\nMOLECULES (21 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_003: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CH3COCOOH (pyruvic acid) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: CH4 (methane) [starting]\n  - mol_006: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: CH3CHO (acetaldehyde) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: CH3CH(NH2)CN (alaninonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: CH3CH(NH2)COOH (DL-alanine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_010: [DL-alanine]_L-enriched (L-alanine) [target]\n  - mol_011: C2H2 (acetylene) [starting]\n  - mol_012: H2O (water) [starting]\n  - mol_0