,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Imine undergoes nucleophilic attack by HCN to form 2-aminopropanenitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Standard Strecker pathway, extensively studied (Miller, 1955, 1957).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_010\",\n      \"name\": \"Alanine Strecker aminonitrile hydrolysis\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_007\", \"mol_008\", \"mol_008\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_009\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"298-350K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"neutral to slightly acidic\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Aminonitrile undergoes two-step hydrolysis to give DL-alanine and release ammonia.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Kinetics and yields confirmed by Miller (1957); the mechanism and mass balance are correct.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_011\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyanosulfidic UV photochemistry to aminonitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_008\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_007\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV radiation\", \"H2S\", \"Cu+ ions\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"298-310K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"strong UV, cyanosulfidic mixture\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"UV-excited cyanosulfidic chemistry generates aminonitrile intermediates from HCN, NH3 and H2O.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Patel et al. (2015, Nature Chemistry) demonstrates this; product is alaninonitrile, not directly alanine.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_012\",\n      \"name\": \"Fischer\u2013Tropsch-type (FTT) synthesis of alanine (CO/H2/NH3, Fe/Ni-meteorite catalyzed)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_015\", \"mol_002\", \"mol_003\", \"mol_008\"],\n 